# Monorepo

This repository is an npm workspaces monorepo:

- `apps/backend` — Express + PostgreSQL API (`@ai-workflow/backend`)
- `apps/frontend` — React + Vite SPA (`@ai-workflow/frontend`)

## Commands (run from repo root)

```bash
npm run dev:backend      # API on :3000
npm run dev:frontend     # SPA on :5173 (proxies /api to backend)
npm run typecheck        # all workspaces
npm run lint             # all workspaces
npm run test             # backend integration tests
```

## Boundaries

- Backend owns persistence, auth tokens, and business rules.
- Frontend owns UI state, routing, and API consumption only.
- Shared types live in each app; do not create a shared package unless a human approves it.
- Run quality checks from the repo root before finishing any task.

## Agent customization

- **Rules** (this folder): short, always-on or file-scoped constraints.
- **Skills**: architecture overviews in `apps/<app>/.cursor/skills/`; deep, per-library
  patterns and the `/new-resource` scaffold in the top-level `.cursor/skills/`.
- Repo-wide skills live in `.agents/skills/` (code review, security).
- There is no `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` — this rules + skills setup is the single source
  of truth for both humans and agents.

See [Cursor Rules](https://cursor.com/docs/rules.md) and [Agent Skills](https://cursor.com/docs/skills.md).
